    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d738">

                <pb facs="0821" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.199/15a: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in
                        France</hi><anchor n="46" xml:id="d738-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-19T10:00:00-04:00">September 19, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On September 14, Consul Chapman acting on instructions from the Department closed
                    Consulate at Bilbao and departed with American members of staff aboard the U. S.
                    S. <hi rendition="#italic">Kane</hi>. Last night the Department instructed
                    Consul Graves to close Malaga Consulate and depart with American staff aboard U.
                    S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Hatfield.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d738-f1" n="46" type="source" xml:id="d738-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also to the Embassy at Madrid and all Consulates except Bilbao and Malaga;
                    also to the Embassy at Paris with instructions to repeat to all seaport
                    Consulates in France, and to the Legation at Lisbon with instructions to inform
                    Consulate and Oporto.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
